IEEE 802.11bn UHR
=================

The dissector handles UHR Operation (extension 151), UHR Capabilities
(extension 152), SMD information (extension 154), UHR Mode Change controls
(extension 157), and Protected UHR action headers.

Reference layout
----------------

The wlan.uhr_layout preference selects one of two layouts:

    d1_5       IEEE 802.11bn D1.5 (default)
    pre_d1_5   Earlier layout from Linux revision 410d70acf9ca

The selected layout is shown in wlan.uhr.layout. The draft version is not
carried in these elements.

D1.5 removed the Basic UHR MCS/NSS Set from Operation and changed the
presence bits and the NPCA, P-EDCA and DBE layouts. An Operation element
containing only two control octets can therefore be valid in D1.5.

Optional fields are located using presence bits, independently of feature
enable bits. AP DBE capability parameters are parsed in Beacon, Probe
Response, Association Response and Reassociation Response frames.

DUO internal fields, DBE MCS/NSS map contents, mode-specific data and
action variable bodies remain raw. Parsing stops where an unsupported
field prevents determining the next offset.

Examples
--------

    tshark -o wlan.uhr_layout:d1_5 -r capture.pcapng
    tshark -o wlan.uhr_layout:pre_d1_5 -r capture.pcapng

Useful filters:

    wlan.uhr.operation.npca_ena
    wlan.uhr.capabilities.mac.npca_supp
    wlan.uhr.truncated

